<!--
  AN-01 - a 1.32 m household android.

  Built on the `feminine_humanoid` package (core / `light` variant): a parametric shell whose
  cross-sections are SUPERELLIPSES lofted along the body with PCHIP interpolation, so the
  surface is continuous rather than a stack of chamfered boxes. Those meshes are the whole
  reason this model looks the way it does, and they are why the earlier hand-built version
  made of MuJoCo primitives could not: a waist-to-hip transition assembled from ellipsoids has
  seams, and the seams are exactly what reads as "mechanical".

  The package's own account of what removes the inorganic look, worth keeping in view when
  editing: the superellipse exponent n is the single roundness knob (n=2 is a true ellipse,
  n>3 approaches a box, and it holds 2.05-2.25), girth varies with height to cut the waist and
  flare the hips, and section centres are offset fore/aft so the chest projects forward while
  the back stays flat. Proportions as authored: B80-W60-H88, waist/hip = 0.68.

  ============================ ORIENTATION: READ THIS FIRST ============================

  The robot faces +x. The face, the chest panel and head_cam all point that way. The source
  URDF is REP-103 (x forward, y left, z up) and so is this, so link origins copy across
  unchanged -- but anything ADDED to the front goes in +x, never in y.

  ========================= WHAT THIS CHANGES FROM THE SOURCE =========================

  1. EVERYTHING IS SCALED BY 0.749. The source stands 1.76 m to the crown with its shoulder
     1.410 m off the floor; this is a 1.32 m robot with the shoulder at 1.056 m.

     Not a style choice. home.xml is built around a MEASURED arm -- drum opening at z=0.91,
     counter at 0.85, basket rim at 0.87 -- and at full size every work surface sits a third
     of a metre below where the arm wants to be. 0.749 is the factor that lands the shoulder
     exactly on 1.056 m. `scale` on each mesh does it at compile time, so the STLs on disk stay
     the package's own and can be refreshed from upstream without re-exporting anything.

  2. IT HAS A FREE JOINT. The source is fixed-base; a walking robot needs a floating pelvis.

  3. IT HAS ACTUATORS, FINGERS AND GRIP SITES. The source is a passive ragdoll (MuJoCo loads
     it with nu=0) whose hands are single rigid links, so nothing about it could grip.
     sim/reach.py aims at sites named `grip_r`/`grip_l`, and brain/laundry.py grasps cloth by
     welding a vertex to the palm -- which needs a palm body and fingers to close on it.

  4. THE JOINT NAMES ARE THE CODEBASE'S. `sh_pitch_r`, not `r_shoulder_pitch`. sim/reach.py's
     ARM_JOINTS and sim/gait.py's stance table are keyed on these, and renaming the model
     rather than the code keeps one convention across four robots.

  5. FOUR SOURCE DOF ARE DROPPED: waist pitch and both wrists. That leaves 24, the same set
     the previous robot had, so the gait and IK are unchanged. Every extra actuated DoF is
     another thing the gait can fight, and none of the dropped ones matter for laundry.

  MASSES ARE THE PACKAGE'S OWN BUDGET and are NOT scaled with the lengths. mass_budget.py
  accounts for shell + actuators + battery/compute + wiring and totals 22.3 kg for the `light`
  variant; those are real components whose mass does not shrink because the robot is shorter.
  Inertias are scaled by 0.749^2, which is what m*L^2 requires when only L changes.

  Two traps, both of which cost time before and are easy to hit again:

    * MuJoCo renders SITES as solid spheres. head_cam sits on the face, so a default-coloured
      site shows up as a bright dot in the middle of it. All sites here are alpha 0.
    * A default-class `rgba` silently overrides every geom's `material` and the whole robot
      renders one flat colour. Defaults set physics; materials set appearance.

  Joint budget (24 actuated DoF):
    legs 2x6 = 12   hip yaw/roll/pitch, knee, ankle pitch/roll
    waist       1   yaw
    neck        2   yaw + pitch
    arms 2x4 = 8    shoulder pitch/roll/yaw, elbow
    grippers 2x1    one actuator per hand, fingers coupled by a tendon
-->
<mujoco model="an01">
  <compiler angle="radian" autolimits="true" meshdir="."/>

  <asset>
    <!-- Shell white with a warm cast, as the package authors it, plus the accent palette from
         the reference render. Colour is functional as well as decorative: grounding.py picks
         the robot out of a frame by colour, so these must not all be the same value. -->
    <material name="a_shell"  rgba="0.930 0.912 0.895 1" specular="0.42" shininess="0.55"/>
    <material name="a_frame"  rgba="0.115 0.115 0.135 1" specular="0.35" shininess="0.55"/>
    <material name="a_blue"   rgba="0.130 0.350 0.850 1" specular="0.70" shininess="0.80"/>
    <material name="a_visor"  rgba="0.060 0.070 0.090 1" specular="0.80" shininess="0.90"/>
    <material name="a_skin"   rgba="0.952 0.898 0.868 1" specular="0.15" shininess="0.25"/>

    <!-- Visual shells, uniform 0.749 scale (see header note 1). -->
    <mesh name="m_base"    file="an01_meshes/base_link.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_waist"   file="an01_meshes/waist_link.stl"  scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_torso"   file="an01_meshes/torso_link.stl"  scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_neck"    file="an01_meshes/neck_link.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_head"    file="an01_meshes/head_link.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_uarm_l"  file="an01_meshes/l_upper_arm.stl" scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_uarm_r"  file="an01_meshes/r_upper_arm.stl" scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_farm_l"  file="an01_meshes/l_forearm.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_farm_r"  file="an01_meshes/r_forearm.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_hand_l"  file="an01_meshes/l_hand.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_hand_r"  file="an01_meshes/r_hand.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_thigh_l" file="an01_meshes/l_thigh.stl"     scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_thigh_r" file="an01_meshes/r_thigh.stl"     scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_shin_l"  file="an01_meshes/l_shin.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_shin_r"  file="an01_meshes/r_shin.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_foot_l"  file="an01_meshes/l_foot.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="m_foot_r"  file="an01_meshes/r_foot.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>

    <!-- Collision hulls: the package's own convex decompositions, same scale. Kept separate
         from the visual meshes on purpose -- the solver wants convex, and the visual shell is
         not convex anywhere interesting. -->
    <mesh name="c_base"    file="an01_collision/base_link.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_torso"   file="an01_collision/torso_link.stl"  scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_head"    file="an01_collision/head_link.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_uarm_l"  file="an01_collision/l_upper_arm.stl" scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_uarm_r"  file="an01_collision/r_upper_arm.stl" scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_farm_l"  file="an01_collision/l_forearm.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_farm_r"  file="an01_collision/r_forearm.stl"   scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_thigh_l" file="an01_collision/l_thigh.stl"     scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_thigh_r" file="an01_collision/r_thigh.stl"     scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_shin_l"  file="an01_collision/l_shin.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_shin_r"  file="an01_collision/r_shin.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_foot_l"  file="an01_collision/l_foot.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
    <mesh name="c_foot_r"  file="an01_collision/r_foot.stl"      scale="0.749 0.749 0.749"/>
  </asset>

  <default>
    <default class="an01">
      <geom condim="3" friction="0.9 0.02 0.001" material="a_shell" group="1"/>
      <joint type="hinge" limited="true" damping="1.2" armature="0.012"/>
      <site size="0.010" rgba="0 0 0 0"/>

      <default class="a_leg">
        <joint damping="6.0" armature="0.045"/>
        <!-- See the note on a_arm: tuned for 22.4 kg, not the 38 kg of the previous model. -->
        <position kp="420" kv="34" forcerange="-180 180"/>
      </default>
      <default class="a_arm">
        <joint damping="2.0" armature="0.020"/>
        <!-- Gains are sized to THIS model's masses, which are the package's own budget and
             LIGHTER than the primitive model they replaced: 22.4 kg against 38. Gains carried
             over from the heavier model are effectively far too stiff, and the failure does
             not look like stiffness -- it looks like a kinematics bug. Measured joint
             velocities of 42-67 rad/s while merely standing, and reach errors above 1 m for
             targets 0.25 m away, purely from servo oscillation. Raising kp made it worse,
             which is the tell. -->
        <position kp="150" kv="16" forcerange="-60 60"/>
      </default>
      <default class="a_finger">
        <joint damping="0.20" armature="0.004"/>
        <position kp="26" kv="1.6" forcerange="-12 12"/>
      </default>
      <!-- The visible shell. contype/conaffinity 0 keeps it out of the contact solver; the
           convex hulls below do the colliding. mass 0 because the <inertial> on each body is
           the package's measured budget and must not be added to by geometry. -->
      <default class="a_skin">
        <geom contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="1" mass="0"/>
      </default>
      <!-- Collision proxies: present to the solver, invisible to the renderer. -->
      <default class="a_hull">
        <geom group="3" rgba="0 0 0 0" mass="0"/>
      </default>
      <default class="a_hullfoot">
        <geom group="3" rgba="0 0 0 0" mass="0"
              condim="4" friction="1.35 0.03 0.002" priority="2"/>
      </default>
      <!-- Small cosmetic details (face, ear pods) that the package mesh does not carry. -->
      <default class="a_deco">
        <geom contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="2" mass="0"/>
      </default>
    </default>
  </default>

  <worldbody>
    <!-- Pelvis rides at 0.738: the sole sits that far below base_link at this scale, so this
         is the height at which the feet just touch the floor. -->
    <body name="pelvis" pos="0 0 0.738" childclass="an01">
      <freejoint name="root"/>
      <site name="imu" pos="0 0 0"/>
      <inertial pos="-0.0034 0 0.0129" mass="4.325"
                diaginertia="0.011667 0.007110 0.006276"/>
      <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_base"/>
      <geom class="a_hull" name="pelvis_g" type="mesh" mesh="c_base"/>

      <!-- ===================== TORSO ===================== -->
      <!-- Source: waist_yaw at base+0.12324, then waist_pitch (dropped) at the same point. The
           waist shell is a short link between them and rides with the torso here. -->
      <body name="torso" pos="0 0 0.09231">
        <!-- Heavily damped on purpose. The torso's yaw inertia is small (izz=0.013) so a servo
             sized by eye rings: measured waist_yaw alone at 20 rad/s while standing still,
             the largest single contributor to a robot that would not settle. -->
        <joint name="waist_yaw" axis="0 0 1" range="-0.70 0.70" damping="9.0" armature="0.05"/>
        <inertial pos="-0.0098 0 0.1515" mass="3.664"
                  diaginertia="0.027232 0.016971 0.012798"/>
        <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_waist"/>
        <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_torso"/>
        <geom class="a_hull" name="chest_g" type="mesh" mesh="c_torso"/>

        <!-- UPPER CHEST AND NECK BASE. Not decoration -- it fills a real hole.

             The package's torso mesh stops at local z=+0.117 and is still 0.074 m wide there:
             it is cut off across the shoulders, not tapered to a neck. The package expects the
             shoulder LINKS to occupy that space, but ours are placed lower (their own mesh
             origins sit at z=0.226), so nothing covered local z=0.117..0.262 and the head
             floated on a visible 0.146 m of nothing.

             The gap is in the SOURCE too -- unscaled, its torso ends at 0.280 and its neck
             starts at 0.430 -- so this is not an artefact of scaling or of the dropped waist
             pitch. It is simply a part the shell generator does not emit.

             Three stacked sections, tapering from the torso's width up to the neck ring, so
             the shoulder line reads as one continuous surface rather than a stack of caps. -->
        <geom class="a_deco" type="ellipsoid" size="0.070 0.092 0.046" pos="0 0 0.140"/>
        <geom class="a_deco" type="ellipsoid" size="0.062 0.098 0.044" pos="0 0 0.196"/>
        <geom class="a_deco" type="ellipsoid" size="0.048 0.060 0.038" pos="0 0 0.238"/>
        <!-- Neck ring: the dark collar the head sits in, closing the last few millimetres. -->
        <geom class="a_deco" type="cylinder" size="0.032 0.020" pos="0 0 0.262"
              material="a_frame"/>

        <!-- Chest indicator panel and blue shoulder discs: from the reference render, not the
             package mesh, which is a bare shell. -->
        <geom class="a_deco" type="box" size="0.006 0.030 0.013" pos="0.084 0 0.208"
              material="a_visor"/>
        <geom class="a_deco" type="box" size="0.003 0.017 0.006" pos="0.089 0 0.208"
              material="a_blue"/>
        <geom class="a_deco" type="cylinder" size="0.030 0.006" pos="0 0.112 0.226"
              euler="1.5708 0 0" material="a_blue"/>
        <geom class="a_deco" type="cylinder" size="0.030 0.006" pos="0 -0.112 0.226"
              euler="1.5708 0 0" material="a_blue"/>

        <!-- ===================== HEAD ===================== -->
        <!-- Source: neck_yaw at torso+0.35392, head_pitch a further 0.04424 up. Both axes sit
             at the neck base so the head pivots on the neck, not about its own centre. -->
        <body name="head" pos="0 0 0.29823">
          <joint name="neck_yaw" axis="0 0 1" pos="0 0 -0.033" range="-1.40 1.40"
                 damping="0.35" armature="0.006"/>
          <joint name="neck_pitch" axis="0 1 0" pos="0 0 -0.033" range="-0.50 0.60"
                 damping="0.35" armature="0.006"/>
          <inertial pos="0.0223 0 0.0631" mass="0.493"
                    diaginertia="0.000448 0.000640 0.000528"/>
          <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_neck" material="a_frame"/>
          <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_head" material="a_skin"/>
          <geom class="a_hull" name="head_g" type="mesh" mesh="c_head"/>

          <!-- NO FACE, NO HAIR, by request. The package head mesh above is left as bare
               shell, which is what it is: a blank ovoid from a shell generator.

               Everything that used to be here -- a blonde bob built from four ellipsoids, and
               two five-part eyes (sclera, iris, pupil, catchlight, lash) -- has been removed
               rather than commented out. It is recoverable from git if wanted, and leaving a
               large block of disabled geometry in the file is how models accumulate parts
               nobody dares delete.

               If a face is added back, measure the mesh FIRST. It spans x -0.057..0.057,
               y -0.072..0.069, z -0.080..0.081 in link-local coordinates, CENTRED ON z=0 --
               not on the crown. Placing features at the z where a primitive skull would have
               had them buries them inside this one. -->

          <!-- Forward-looking camera, between the eyes. alpha 0: see the header. -->
          <camera name="head_cam" pos="0.064 0 0.000" euler="0 -1.5708 1.5708" fovy="70"/>
          <site name="head_cam_site" pos="0.064 0 0.000"/>

          <!-- Side cameras, 60 degrees out from forward with a 90-degree field, so the pair
               covers what the 70-degree head camera cannot see. sim/robot.side_clearance
               reads them to decide whether the robot fits past something.

               They are NOT optional for a robot that navigates. MaplessNavigator calls
               side_clearance on every approach step, and without these the whole errand dies
               with `The camera "look_left" does not exist` the moment vision navigation is
               used -- which is exactly what happened when this model first drove a laundry
               run. Same names and same angles as pyunto_h1, because the code addresses them
               by name and the geometry is what the percentile reading was tuned against. -->
          <camera name="look_left" pos="0.040 0.040 0.000" xyaxes="0.866 -0.5 0 0 0 1"
                  fovy="90"/>
          <camera name="look_right" pos="0.040 -0.040 0.000" xyaxes="-0.866 -0.5 0 0 0 1"
                  fovy="90"/>
        </body>

        <!-- ===================== RIGHT ARM ===================== -->
        <!-- Source: r_shoulder_* at torso+(0, -0.14220, 0.30178), the three axes coincident. -->
        <body name="shoulder_r" pos="0 -0.10651 0.22603">
          <joint name="sh_pitch_r" axis="0 1 0" range="-3.00 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
          <!-- Roll is limited PER SIDE so the arm cannot swing across the chest.

               The source URDF's own limits are asymmetric for exactly this reason. Copying a
               symmetric +-1.70 to both sides instead let each arm reach through the torso, and
               the IK duly found those solutions: measured reach errors of 1.0-1.7 m for
               targets 0.25 m away, because the solver was driving the hand round the far side
               of the body rather than out in front of it. A joint limit is part of the
               kinematics, not a safety margin. -->
          <joint name="sh_roll_r" axis="1 0 0" range="-2.20 0.25" class="a_arm"/>
          <joint name="sh_yaw_r" axis="0 0 1" range="-1.80 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
          <inertial pos="0 0 -0.1834" mass="1.427"
                    diaginertia="0.001451 0.001446 0.000065"/>
          <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_uarm_r"/>
          <geom class="a_hull" name="uarm_r" type="mesh" mesh="c_uarm_r"/>

          <body name="forearm_r" pos="0 0 -0.20947">
            <joint name="elbow_r" axis="0 1 0" range="-2.40 0.05" class="a_arm"/>
            <inertial pos="0 0 -0.0576" mass="0.423"
                      diaginertia="0.000256 0.000252 0.000035"/>
            <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_farm_r"/>
            <geom class="a_hull" name="farm_r" type="mesh" mesh="c_farm_r"/>

            <!-- Hand. The package hand is one rigid link with no fingers, which cannot grip:
                 brain/laundry.py grasps cloth by welding a vertex to the PALM, and needs
                 fingers to close on it for the contact that triggers the weld. So the package
                 mesh stays as the visible hand, and a palm with two tendon-coupled fingers is
                 built at the wrist. -->
            <body name="palm_r" pos="0 0 -0.16450">
              <inertial pos="0 0 -0.0552" mass="0.042"
                        diaginertia="0.000043 0.000050 0.000014"/>
              <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_hand_r"/>
              <geom class="a_hull" name="palm_r_g" type="box" size="0.011 0.026 0.030"
                    pos="0 0 -0.026"/>
              <!-- The IK target. sim/reach.py aims THIS site, not the palm body. -->
              <site name="grip_r" pos="0 0 -0.050"/>

              <body name="finger_r1" pos="0 -0.022 -0.050">
                <joint name="grip_r1" axis="1 0 0" range="0 0.9" class="a_finger"/>
                <inertial pos="0 0 -0.015" mass="0.02" diaginertia="5e-6 5e-6 5e-6"/>
                <geom name="fing_r1" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                      fromto="0 0 0 0 0.003 -0.032"/>
              </body>
              <body name="finger_r2" pos="0 0.022 -0.050">
                <joint name="grip_r2" axis="-1 0 0" range="0 0.9" class="a_finger"/>
                <inertial pos="0 0 -0.015" mass="0.02" diaginertia="5e-6 5e-6 5e-6"/>
                <geom name="fing_r2" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                      fromto="0 0 0 0 -0.003 -0.032"/>
              </body>
            </body>
          </body>
        </body>

        <!-- ===================== LEFT ARM ===================== -->
        <body name="shoulder_l" pos="0 0.10651 0.22603">
          <joint name="sh_pitch_l" axis="0 1 0" range="-3.00 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
          <joint name="sh_roll_l" axis="1 0 0" range="-0.25 2.20" class="a_arm"/>
          <joint name="sh_yaw_l" axis="0 0 1" range="-1.80 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
          <inertial pos="0 0 -0.1834" mass="1.427"
                    diaginertia="0.001451 0.001446 0.000065"/>
          <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_uarm_l"/>
          <geom class="a_hull" name="uarm_l" type="mesh" mesh="c_uarm_l"/>

          <body name="forearm_l" pos="0 0 -0.20947">
            <joint name="elbow_l" axis="0 1 0" range="-2.40 0.05" class="a_arm"/>
            <inertial pos="0 0 -0.0576" mass="0.423"
                      diaginertia="0.000256 0.000252 0.000035"/>
            <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_farm_l"/>
            <geom class="a_hull" name="farm_l" type="mesh" mesh="c_farm_l"/>

            <body name="palm_l" pos="0 0 -0.16450">
              <inertial pos="0 0 -0.0552" mass="0.042"
                        diaginertia="0.000043 0.000050 0.000014"/>
              <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_hand_l"/>
              <geom class="a_hull" name="palm_l_g" type="box" size="0.011 0.026 0.030"
                    pos="0 0 -0.026"/>
              <site name="grip_l" pos="0 0 -0.050"/>

              <body name="finger_l1" pos="0 -0.022 -0.050">
                <joint name="grip_l1" axis="1 0 0" range="0 0.9" class="a_finger"/>
                <inertial pos="0 0 -0.015" mass="0.02" diaginertia="5e-6 5e-6 5e-6"/>
                <geom name="fing_l1" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                      fromto="0 0 0 0 0.003 -0.032"/>
              </body>
              <body name="finger_l2" pos="0 0.022 -0.050">
                <joint name="grip_l2" axis="-1 0 0" range="0 0.9" class="a_finger"/>
                <inertial pos="0 0 -0.015" mass="0.02" diaginertia="5e-6 5e-6 5e-6"/>
                <geom name="fing_l2" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                      fromto="0 0 0 0 -0.003 -0.032"/>
              </body>
            </body>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>

      <!-- ===================== RIGHT LEG ===================== -->
      <!-- Source: r_hip_* at base+(0, -0.07742, 0), the three axes coincident. -->
      <body name="hip_r" pos="0 -0.05799 0">
        <joint name="hip_yaw_r" axis="0 0 1" range="-0.70 0.70" class="a_leg" damping="12.0"/>
        <joint name="hip_roll_r" axis="1 0 0" range="-0.70 0.50" class="a_leg"/>
        <joint name="hip_pitch_r" axis="0 1 0" range="-2.00 1.00" class="a_leg"/>
        <inertial pos="0 0 -0.2831" mass="3.519"
                  diaginertia="0.009472 0.009441 0.000486"/>
        <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_thigh_r"/>
        <geom class="a_hull" name="thigh_r" type="mesh" mesh="c_thigh_r"/>

        <body name="shin_r" pos="0 0 -0.32426">
          <joint name="knee_r" axis="0 1 0" range="0 2.40" class="a_leg"/>
          <inertial pos="0 0 -0.0754" mass="1.396"
                    diaginertia="0.001754 0.001741 0.000165"/>
          <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_shin_r"/>
          <geom class="a_hull" name="shin_r_g" type="mesh" mesh="c_shin_r"/>

          <body name="foot_r" pos="0 0 -0.26982">
            <joint name="ank_pitch_r" axis="0 1 0" range="-1.00 0.70" class="a_leg"/>
            <joint name="ank_roll_r" axis="1 0 0" range="-0.50 0.50" class="a_leg"/>
            <inertial pos="0.0405 0 -0.0374" mass="0.111"
                      diaginertia="0.000058 0.000247 0.000263"/>
            <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_foot_r"/>
            <!-- A REAL SOLE, replacing the package's foot hull for collision purposes.

                 The package foot is 0.055 m long and 0.066 m wide -- a peg, narrower than it
                 is tall (0.173). A 22 kg robot balancing on two patches that size cannot
                 stand still: measured the pelvis oscillating 0.022 m peak-to-peak, with the
                 ankles as the largest contributors (ank_roll 0.096 rad), because the support
                 polygon was too small for the ankle servos to have any leverage against.

                 This box is a foot: 0.19 x 0.085, heel behind the ankle and toe in front of
                 it, which is what gives the pitch axis a moment arm to push against. The
                 package mesh stays as the VISIBLE foot -- only the contact shape changes. -->
            <geom class="a_hullfoot" name="foot_r_g" type="box"
                  size="0.095 0.0425 0.012" pos="0.026 0 -0.063"/>
            <site name="sole_r" pos="0.040 0 -0.056"/>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>

      <!-- ===================== LEFT LEG ===================== -->
      <body name="hip_l" pos="0 0.05799 0">
        <joint name="hip_yaw_l" axis="0 0 1" range="-0.70 0.70" class="a_leg" damping="12.0"/>
        <joint name="hip_roll_l" axis="1 0 0" range="-0.50 0.70" class="a_leg"/>
        <joint name="hip_pitch_l" axis="0 1 0" range="-2.00 1.00" class="a_leg"/>
        <inertial pos="0 0 -0.2831" mass="3.519"
                  diaginertia="0.009472 0.009441 0.000486"/>
        <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_thigh_l"/>
        <geom class="a_hull" name="thigh_l" type="mesh" mesh="c_thigh_l"/>

        <body name="shin_l" pos="0 0 -0.32426">
          <joint name="knee_l" axis="0 1 0" range="0 2.40" class="a_leg"/>
          <inertial pos="0 0 -0.0754" mass="1.396"
                    diaginertia="0.001754 0.001741 0.000165"/>
          <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_shin_l"/>
          <geom class="a_hull" name="shin_l_g" type="mesh" mesh="c_shin_l"/>

          <body name="foot_l" pos="0 0 -0.26982">
            <joint name="ank_pitch_l" axis="0 1 0" range="-1.00 0.70" class="a_leg"/>
            <joint name="ank_roll_l" axis="1 0 0" range="-0.50 0.50" class="a_leg"/>
            <inertial pos="0.0405 0 -0.0374" mass="0.111"
                      diaginertia="0.000058 0.000247 0.000263"/>
            <geom class="a_skin" type="mesh" mesh="m_foot_l"/>
            <!-- A REAL SOLE, replacing the package's foot hull for collision purposes.

                 The package foot is 0.055 m long and 0.066 m wide -- a peg, narrower than it
                 is tall (0.173). A 22 kg robot balancing on two patches that size cannot
                 stand still: measured the pelvis oscillating 0.022 m peak-to-peak, with the
                 ankles as the largest contributors (ank_roll 0.096 rad), because the support
                 polygon was too small for the ankle servos to have any leverage against.

                 This box is a foot: 0.19 x 0.085, heel behind the ankle and toe in front of
                 it, which is what gives the pitch axis a moment arm to push against. The
                 package mesh stays as the VISIBLE foot -- only the contact shape changes. -->
            <geom class="a_hullfoot" name="foot_l_g" type="box"
                  size="0.095 0.0425 0.012" pos="0.026 0 -0.063"/>
            <site name="sole_l" pos="0.040 0 -0.056"/>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <!-- Fingers move together on one actuator: a two-finger pinch does not need independent
       control, and one command per hand is what brain/skills.py issues. -->
  <tendon>
    <fixed name="grip_r_t">
      <joint joint="grip_r1" coef="1"/>
      <joint joint="grip_r2" coef="-1"/>
    </fixed>
    <fixed name="grip_l_t">
      <joint joint="grip_l1" coef="1"/>
      <joint joint="grip_l2" coef="-1"/>
    </fixed>
  </tendon>
  <equality>
    <tendon tendon1="grip_r_t"/>
    <tendon tendon1="grip_l_t"/>
  </equality>

  <actuator>
    <!-- neck (2) -->
    <position name="neck_yaw" joint="neck_yaw" ctrlrange="-1.40 1.40" kp="25" kv="2.5"/>
    <!-- Pitch carries the head against gravity, so it needs more than yaw. Everything this
         robot works with -- drum, basket, counter -- is below eye level. -->
    <position name="neck_pitch" joint="neck_pitch" ctrlrange="-0.50 0.60" kp="35" kv="3.0"/>

    <!-- legs (12) -->
    <position name="hip_yaw_r" joint="hip_yaw_r" ctrlrange="-0.70 0.70" kp="200" kv="26" forcerange="-180 180"/>
    <position name="hip_roll_r" joint="hip_roll_r" ctrlrange="-0.70 0.50" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="hip_pitch_r" joint="hip_pitch_r" ctrlrange="-2.00 1.00" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="knee_r" joint="knee_r" ctrlrange="0 2.40" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="ank_pitch_r" joint="ank_pitch_r" ctrlrange="-1.00 0.70" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="ank_roll_r" joint="ank_roll_r" ctrlrange="-0.50 0.50" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="hip_yaw_l" joint="hip_yaw_l" ctrlrange="-0.70 0.70" kp="200" kv="26" forcerange="-180 180"/>
    <position name="hip_roll_l" joint="hip_roll_l" ctrlrange="-0.50 0.70" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="hip_pitch_l" joint="hip_pitch_l" ctrlrange="-2.00 1.00" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="knee_l" joint="knee_l" ctrlrange="0 2.40" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="ank_pitch_l" joint="ank_pitch_l" ctrlrange="-1.00 0.70" class="a_leg"/>
    <position name="ank_roll_l" joint="ank_roll_l" ctrlrange="-0.50 0.50" class="a_leg"/>

    <!-- waist (1) -->
    <position name="waist_yaw" joint="waist_yaw" ctrlrange="-0.70 0.70" kp="60" kv="14"/>

    <!-- arms (8) -->
    <position name="sh_pitch_r" joint="sh_pitch_r" ctrlrange="-3.00 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="sh_roll_r" joint="sh_roll_r" ctrlrange="-2.20 0.25" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="sh_yaw_r" joint="sh_yaw_r" ctrlrange="-1.80 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="elbow_r" joint="elbow_r" ctrlrange="-2.40 0.05" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="sh_pitch_l" joint="sh_pitch_l" ctrlrange="-3.00 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="sh_roll_l" joint="sh_roll_l" ctrlrange="-0.25 2.20" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="sh_yaw_l" joint="sh_yaw_l" ctrlrange="-1.80 1.80" class="a_arm"/>
    <position name="elbow_l" joint="elbow_l" ctrlrange="-2.40 0.05" class="a_arm"/>

    <!-- grippers (2) -->
    <position name="grip_r" joint="grip_r1" ctrlrange="0 0.9" class="a_finger"/>
    <position name="grip_l" joint="grip_l1" ctrlrange="0 0.9" class="a_finger"/>
  </actuator>
</mujoco>
